  "construction": "Surface code of the orientably-regular map R82.22 of type {6,6} (genus 82) in M. Conder's list of reflexible maps of genus 2 to 301. Rotation group G = <r,s | r^6, s^6, (r*s)^2, s*r*s^-2*r^3*s^3*r^-2, r*s^-2*r*s^-1*r^2*s^-2*r*s^-1*r, s*r*s^-1*r^-1*s*r^2*s*r^-1*s^-1*r*s> of order 972. Darts = elements of G (right multiplication), faces = cosets g<r>, vertices = cosets g<s>, edges = cosets g<rs> = {g, grs}. Qubits on the 486 edges, X-checks on the 162 vertices (weight 6), Z-checks on the 162 faces (weight 6), incidences mod 2: H_X and H_Z are the boundary maps of the cellular chain complex over F_2, k = 2 - chi = 164, d_Z is the shortest homologically nontrivial cycle of the map and d_X that of the dual map. Found in a census of regular maps (normal subgroups of the triangle groups <r,s | r^p, s^q, (rs)^2>, Magma's LowIndexNormalSubgroups). The qubit order is that of the dart permutations in the public package in the references (data/maps.json), whose src/rebuild.py rebuilds these matrices from them and from the presentation.",
